<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: vector, indexing, min,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	Given a starting vertex, this function computes both the shortest distance and path to every other vertex in a directed graph &lt;pf&gt;G&lt;/pf&gt;.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>G</pf> (struct) number — : A structure representing the directed graph.</p>
			<p><pf>source</pf> (integer) integer — : The index of the source vertex from which shortest paths are calculated.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>distances</pf> (1 x n) double vector — : A row vector where each element <pf>distances(i)</pf> represents the shortest distance from the source vertex to vertex <pf>i</pf>. If a vertex is unreachable, its distance is <pf>inf</pf>.</p>
			<p><pf>paths</pf> (1 x n) double vector — : A cell array where each element <pf>paths{i}</pf> is a vector representing the shortest path from the source vertex to vertex <pf>i</pf>.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Ensure your function handles cases with no edges (empty edge list).</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>In MATLAB, cell arrays are like matrices, except you can store different types of objects. This new structure is needed to store each path as a vector.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Command Window Expected Output V = 1:6; E = [ 1 2 1; 1 3 7; 1 4 6; 2 3 2; 3 4 8; 3 5 3; 4 5 4; 4 6 6; 5 6 4 ]; G = HW6P5_construct_directed_graph(V,E,'G'); [distances, paths] = HW6P7_min_cost_paths(G,1) distances = 0 1 3 6 6 10 paths = {[1], [1 2], [1 2 3], [1 4], ... [1 2 3 5], [1 2 3 5 6]} V = 1:4; E = [ 1 2 3; 1 3 1; 2 4 2; 3 4 6 ]; G = HW6P5_construct_directed_graph(V,E,'G'); [distances, paths] = HW6P7_min_cost_paths(G,1) distances = 0 3 1 5 paths = {[1], [1 2], [1 3], [1 2 4]} V = 1:3; E = [ 1 2 5; 2 3 4 ]; <pf>G = HW6P5_construct_directed_graph(V,E,'G');</pf> [distances, paths] = HW6P<pf>7_min_cost_paths</pf>(G,2); distances = Inf 0 4 paths = {0×0 double, [2], [2 3]} V = 1:3; E = []; <pf>G = HW6P5_construct_directed_graph(V,E,'G');</pf> [distances, paths] = HW6P<pf>7_min_cost_paths</pf>(G,3); distances = Inf Inf 0 paths = {0×0 double, 0×0 double, [3]}</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Expected Output</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>distances = 0 1 3 6 6 10 paths = {[1], [1 2], [1 2 3], [1 4], ... [1 2 3 5], [1 2 3 5 6]}</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>distances = 0 3 1 5 paths = {[1], [1 2], [1 3], [1 2 4]}</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>distances = Inf 0 4 paths = {0×0 double, [2], [2 3]}</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>distances = Inf Inf 0 paths = {0×0 double, 0×0 double, [3]}</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
